# Vercel falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent -- and the repo ignores
# web/public/patch/* (the patch is a build artifact, never committed). That is why the
# first deploy went up with no BPS at all: the shell fetched /patch/br-version.json,
# got a 404, and told everybody "no patch published yet -- starting the unpatched ROM".
#
# So this file exists to say the opposite of .gitignore for that one directory, and to
# keep saying it for the one file in there that must NEVER be published.
node_modules
dist
test-results
playwright-report
e2e
.env*
.vercel

# The dev ROM. tools/br/dev-patch.sh leaves a full, patched, copyrighted Emerald in
# public/patch/ so the dev shell can skip the file picker; app.ts only ever fetches it
# under import.meta.env.DEV and says so in its own comment: "nothing ships this file".
# Nothing enforced that until now. The ROM lives on the player's device and nowhere else.
public/patch/pokeemerald.gba
*.gba
*.sav
*.ss?
